    ('APO12-WP15', 'APO12', 'Risk-related root causes', 'Part of the risk assessment and risk reporting process', 188),
    ('APO13-WP1', 'APO13', 'ISMS policy', 'There will be either a policy, standard or operating practice that will be part of the information security management system.', 189),
    ('APO13-WP2', 'APO13', 'ISMS scope statement', 'Part of the ISMS strategy and planning documentation or the ISMS programme outline', 190),
    ('APO13-WP3', 'APO13', 'Information security risk treatment plan', 'Part of the ISMS risk assessment process based on the risk profile', 191),
    ('APO13-WP4', 'APO13', 'Information security business cases', 'Only if required for an information security project or programme', 192),
    ('APO13-WP5', 'APO13', 'ISMS audit reports', 'Part of internal audit reporting or monthly information security reporting, which will also be integrated into a security incident response and reporting system.', 193),
    ('APO13-WP6', 'APO13', 'Recommendations for improving the ISMS', 'Part of normal ISMS monitoring and reporting. Assessors should look for or ask for this.', 194),
    ('BAI01-WP1', 'BAI01', 'Updated programme and project management approaches', 'Part of the organisation’s project/programme management information (PM) system or framework', 195),
    ('BAI01-WP2', 'BAI01', 'Stakeholder engagement plan', 'Part of the portfolio management process', 196),
    ('BAI01-WP3', 'BAI01', 'Results of stakeholder engagement effectiveness assessments', 'Part of the portfolio management process and periodic project and programme management reporting', 197),
    ('BAI01-WP4', 'BAI01', 'Programme concept business case', 'Usually the first, high-level business case produced at a programme level. Once noted and approved to go to the next stage, and after more analysis and feasibility studies, a more detailed business case is done and broken down to project level.', 198),
    ('BAI01-WP5', 'BAI01', 'Programme mandate and brief', 'Part of the project/programme manager’s office (PMO) setup and process, and creates the charter to set up a project or programme', 199),
    ('BAI01-WP6', 'BAI01', 'Programme benefit realisation plan', 'A precursor to the business case and would normally be part of that analysis', 200),
    ('BAI01-WP7', 'BAI01', 'Programme plan', 'Produced by the programme manager and is detailed enough to show costs, benefits, resourcing, timelines, dependencies and risk analysis', 201),
    ('BAI01-WP8', 'BAI01', 'Programme budget and benefits register', 'A key part of the PMO setup and process and a source of input for business cases, benefits realisation planning, and programme and project management', 202),
    ('BAI01-WP9', 'BAI01', 'Resource requirements and roles', 'Part of the PMO setup and process and creates the charter to set up a project or programme', 203),
    ('BAI01-WP10', 'BAI01', 'Results of benefit realisation monitoring', 'Part of the PMO setup and process and should be incorporated into the monthly project and programme monitoring and reporting', 204),
    ('BAI01-WP11', 'BAI01', 'Results of programme goal achievement monitoring', 'Part of the PMO setup and process and should be incorporated into the monthly project and programme monitoring and reporting', 205),
    ('BAI01-WP12', 'BAI01', 'Results of programme performance reviews', 'Part of the PMO setup and process and should be incorporated into the monthly project and programme monitoring and reporting', 206),
    ('BAI01-WP13', 'BAI01', 'Stage-gate review results', 'A stage-gate process is a conceptual and operational road map for moving a new-product project from idea to launch. Stage-gate divides the effort into distinct stages separated by management decision gates. For example, some are organised around a project life cycle (appraise, select, define, execute and operate), some by project phases. A decision must be made at each gate before the project or programme can progress. Assessors should look for the reviews of these decisions.', 207),
    ('BAI01-WP14', 'BAI01', 'Project plans', 'Part of the normal PMO setup and process', 208),
    ('BAI01-WP15', 'BAI01', 'Project baseline', 'Part of project planning and is done at the project start-up and at periodic intervals decided on by the PMO', 209),
    ('BAI01-WP16', 'BAI01', 'Project reports and communications', 'Part of the normal PMO setup and process', 210),
    ('BAI01-WP17', 'BAI01', 'Quality management plan', 'Part of the normal PMO setup and process', 211),
    ('BAI01-WP18', 'BAI01', 'Requirements for independent verification of deliverables', 'Usually part of the stage-gate reviews. A gate decision maker may ask for this if necessary, but it is dependent on the project or programme.', 212),
    ('BAI01-WP19', 'BAI01', 'Project scope statements', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 213),
    ('BAI01-WP20', 'BAI01', 'Project definitions', 'Self explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 214),
    ('BAI01-WP21', 'BAI01', 'Project risk management plan', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 215),
    ('BAI01-WP22', 'BAI01', 'Project risk assessment results', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 216),
    ('BAI01-WP23', 'BAI01', 'Project risk register', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 217),
    ('BAI01-WP24', 'BAI01', 'Project performance criteria', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 218),
    ('BAI01-WP25', 'BAI01', 'Project progress reports', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 219),
    ('BAI01-WP26', 'BAI01', 'Agreed-on changes to project plan', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 220),
    ('BAI01-WP27', 'BAI01', 'Project resource requirements', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 221),
    ('BAI01-WP28', 'BAI01', 'Project roles and responsibilities', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 222),
    ('BAI01-WP29', 'BAI01', 'Gaps in project planning', 'Self-explanatory and part of the normal PMO setup and process', 223),
    ('BAI01-WP30', 'BAI01', 'Post-implementation review results', 'Timing is an issue here, usually undertaken after several months of operation', 224),
    ('BAI01-WP31', 'BAI01', 'Project lessons learned', 'Part of the post-implementation review', 225),
    ('BAI01-WP32', 'BAI01', 'Stakeholder project acceptance confirmations', 'Part of the project sign-off and closure', 226),
    ('BAI01-WP33', 'BAI01', 'Communication of programme retirement and ongoing accountabilities', 'Part of the project sign-off and closure', 227),
    ('BAI02-WP1', 'BAI02', 'Requirements definition repository', 'Part of the systems development analysis for new developments and is a log or register holding all business user requirements', 228),
    ('BAI02-WP2', 'BAI02', 'Confirmed acceptance of requirements from stakeholders', 'Usually done as part of a feasibility study report', 229),
    ('BAI02-WP3', 'BAI02', 'Record of requirement change requests', 'Part of a change log for operational change management', 230),
    ('BAI02-WP4', 'BAI02', 'Feasibility study report', 'A comprehensive report that contains user requirements, outline of the solutions for development, risk assessment, capacity and performance planning, etc.', 231),
    ('BAI02-WP5', 'BAI02', 'High-level acquisition/development plan', 'Contains the initial design and development proposal for applications and infrastructure', 232),
    ('BAI02-WP6', 'BAI02', 'Requirements risk register', 'Similar to the IT or enterprise risk management risk register and integrated into the main risk assessment process', 233),
    ('BAI02-WP7', 'BAI02', 'Risk mitigation actions', 'Derived from the requirements risk register', 234),
    ('BAI02-WP8', 'BAI02', 'Sponsor approvals of requirements and proposed solutions', 'There must be evidence of requirements sign-off of both the statement of requirements (SOR) and definitions and the feasibility study report.', 235),
    ('BAI02-WP9', 'BAI02', 'Approved quality reviews', 'Part of the ongoing project development cycle', 236),
    ('BAI03-WP1', 'BAI03', 'Approved high-level design specification', 'Self-explanatory and part of the system development life cycle (SDLC) process', 237),
    ('BAI03-WP2', 'BAI03', 'Approved detailed design specification', 'Self-explanatory and part of the SDLC process', 238),
    ('BAI03-WP3', 'BAI03', 'Documented solution components', 'Self-explanatory and part of the SDLC process', 239),
    ('BAI03-WP4', 'BAI03', 'Approved acquisition plans', 'May be found in the mergers and acquisitions department with copies in the IT department, if predominantly an IT development', 240),
    ('BAI03-WP5', 'BAI03', 'Updates to asset inventory', 'Self-explanatory and should be part of asset inventory procedures', 241),
    ('BAI03-WP6', 'BAI03', 'Integrated and configured solution components', 'Usually undertaken by the accounts department, but instigated by the bringing the new asset into production', 242),
    ('BAI03-WP7', 'BAI03', 'Quality assurance plan', 'Self-explanatory and part of the SDLC process', 243),
    ('BAI03-WP8', 'BAI03', 'Quality review results, exceptions and corrections', 'Self-explanatory and part of the SDLC process', 244),
    ('BAI03-WP9', 'BAI03', 'Test plan', 'Part of the new system changeover planning documents', 245),
    ('BAI03-WP10', 'BAI03', 'Test procedures', 'Part of the new system changeover planning documents', 246),
    ('BAI03-WP11', 'BAI03', 'Test result logs and audit trails', 'Part of the new system changeover planning documents', 247),
    ('BAI03-WP12', 'BAI03', 'Test result communications', 'Part of the new system changeover planning documents', 248),
    ('BAI03-WP13', 'BAI03', 'Record of all approved and applied change requests', 'Found in a change management log', 249),
    ('BAI03-WP14', 'BAI03', 'Maintenance plan', 'Part of the new system changeover planning documents', 250),
    ('BAI03-WP15', 'BAI03', 'Updated solution components and related documentation', 'Usually found in a plan for the maintenance of solution and infrastructure components. Periodic reviews against business needs and the amended operational requirements should be included.', 251),
    ('BAI03-WP16', 'BAI03', 'Periodic maintenance analyses', 'Usually found in a plan for the maintenance of solution and infrastructure components. Periodic reviews against business needs and the amended operational requirements should be included.', 252),
    ('BAI03-WP17', 'BAI03', 'Service definitions', 'Forms part of a service portfolio or catalogue and defines all services including SLAs and OLAs', 253),
    ('BAI03-WP18', 'BAI03', 'Updated service portfolio', 'Needs updating periodically due to normal maintenance and changes in SLAs and OLAs, service offerings, etc.', 254),
    ('BAI04-WP1', 'BAI04', 'Availability, performance and capacity baselines', 'An assessment of system infrastructure and application performance and capacity, is assessed during the development stages and baselined after testing and start-up of the system or process', 255),
    ('BAI04-WP2', 'BAI04', 'Evaluations against SLAs', 'Periodic evaluations, usually monthly, as part of monthly IT reporting and monitoring and uses the service catalogue or portfolio as a reference point', 256),
    ('BAI04-WP3', 'BAI04', 'Prioritised improvements', 'Based on monthly evaluations of system performance', 257),
    ('BAI04-WP4', 'BAI04', 'Performance and capacity plans', 'Produced with baselining during the monthly reporting and monitoring process', 258),
    ('BAI04-WP5', 'BAI04', 'Availability, performance and capacity monitoring review reports', 'Part of the monthly IT monitoring and reporting process', 259),
    ('BAI04-WP6', 'BAI04', 'Performance and capacity gaps', 'Normally logged in a register or log and forms part of the monthly IT monitoring and reporting process', 260),
    ('BAI04-WP7', 'BAI04', 'Corrective actions', 'Shown in the register or log. Assessors should verify that there are follow-up actions as part of the periodic reporting process.', 261),
    ('BAI04-WP8', 'BAI04', 'Emergency escalation procedure', 'Part of the change management process defined in the change management operating practices and or standards', 262),
    ('BAI04-WP9', 'BAI04', 'Availability, performance and capacity scenarios', 'Part of capacity planning and originates during the system development phases through baselining, testing and change over. Will need updating as part of capacity planning and reporting on a periodic basis.', 263),
    ('BAI04-WP10', 'BAI04', 'Availability, performance and capacity business impact assessments', 'Part of the IT risk management assessment process. It will not normally be separate, so assessor should check to see that the risk register includes these impacts.', 264),
    ('BAI05-WP1', 'BAI05', 'Communications of drivers for change', 'Part of the organisation change management process and will include strong business input', 265),
    ('BAI05-WP2', 'BAI05', 'Communications from executive management committing to change', 'Part of the change management process. Business should be accountable for all IT changes; documentation should exist confirming this, usually in the programme or project change management process.', 266),
    ('BAI05-WP3', 'BAI05', 'Implementation team and roles', 'Part of the PMO procedures and programme initiation document', 267),
    ('BAI05-WP4', 'BAI05', 'Common vision and goals', 'Part of the PMO procedures and programme initiation document', 268),
    ('BAI05-WP5', 'BAI05', 'Vision communication plan', 'Part of the programme or project plans, may not be a separate document', 269),
    ('BAI05-WP6', 'BAI05', 'Vision communications', 'Part of the project reporting process', 270),
    ('BAI05-WP7', 'BAI05', 'Aligned HR performance objectives', 'Part of the benefits realisation planning and business case', 271),
    ('BAI05-WP8', 'BAI05', 'Identified quick wins', 'Part of the benefits realisation planning and business case', 272),
    ('BAI05-WP9', 'BAI05', 'Communications of benefits', 'Part of the benefits realisation planning and business case', 273),
    ('BAI05-WP10', 'BAI05', 'Operation and use plan', 'More tactical and typically a plan that outlines the details of how the changes will be used and the operation process around them', 274),
    ('BAI05-WP11', 'BAI05', 'Success measures and results', 'Part of the operation and use plan', 275),
    ('BAI05-WP12', 'BAI05', 'Compliance audit results', 'Assumes an internal audit or formal assessment/evaluation of the change management programme or project', 276),
    ('BAI05-WP13', 'BAI05', 'Awareness communications', 'Part of the change management communication plan', 277),
    ('BAI05-WP14', 'BAI05', 'HR performance review results', 'Part of sustaining the changes. It relates to the effective training of new staff and is typically linked to the annual appraisal process.', 278),
    ('BAI05-WP15', 'BAI05', 'Knowledge transfer plans', 'Part of sustaining the changes. There should be some form of ongoing communication campaigns, continued top management commitment, adoption monitoring and sharing of lessons learned across the enterprise.', 279),
    ('BAI05-WP16', 'BAI05', 'Communications of management’s commitment', 'Part of the organisational change management process. Assessors should confirm that there these communications are documented.', 280),
    ('BAI05-WP17', 'BAI05', 'Reviews of operational use', 'Part of the monthly monitoring and reporting process', 281),
    ('BAI06-WP1', 'BAI06', 'Impact assessments', 'Part of the IT risk management process. Assessor should verify that normal operational change impacts are being captured in the risk register.', 282),
    ('BAI06-WP2', 'BAI06', 'Approved requests for change', 'Documented in a change management log and must have user/requestor authorisation', 283),
    ('BAI06-WP3', 'BAI06', 'Change plan and schedule', 'Part of the change management process. Day-to-day changes will be documented in an annual plan and monthly schedule and will typically include all patch management, normal upgrades, etc.', 284),
    ('BAI06-WP4', 'BAI06', 'Post-implementation review of emergency changes', 'Usually done quarterly as part of the ongoing monitoring and reporting process', 285),
    ('BAI06-WP5', 'BAI06', 'Change request status reports', 'Typically shows where the change is in the cycle, development, test, etc.', 286),
    ('BAI06-WP6', 'BAI06', 'Change documentation', 'Starts with a comprehensive change log or register and will include requests for change, review and approval, feedback to management and initiator. Segregation of duties is an important part of this documentation.', 287),
    ('BAI07-WP1', 'BAI07', 'Approved implementation plan', 'Part of the changeover/cutover planning and includes roles and responsibilities, a detailed schedule of testing and handover procedures', 288),
    ('BAI07-WP2', 'BAI07', 'Implementation fallback and recovery process', 'Part of the implementation plan and a crucial element in the plan', 289),
    ('BAI07-WP3', 'BAI07', 'Migration plan', 'Part of the implementation and documents how both master data and operational data are to be transferred; typically includes both manual and automated processes', 290),
    ('BAI07-WP4', 'BAI07', 'Approved acceptance test plan', 'Usually part of the implementation plan or a subset, but is usually comprehensive enough because it is one of the key phases of system changeover', 291),
    ('BAI07-WP5', 'BAI07', 'Test data', 'Part of test planning; usually requires preparation and decisions on source, live examples or dummy data.', 292),
    ('BAI07-WP6', 'BAI07', 'Test results log', 'Part of the testing process', 293),
    ('BAI07-WP7', 'BAI07', 'Evaluation of results', 'Refers to the test results', 294),
    ('BAI07-WP8', 'BAI07', 'Approved acceptance and release to production', 'Final sign-off is crucial to the successful launch of a new system and comes after the evaluation of test results.', 295),
    ('BAI07-WP9', 'BAI07', 'Release plan', 'Part of the acceptance and approval process', 296),
    ('BAI07-WP10', 'BAI07', 'Release log', 'Optional. Many enterprises will have a release plan without a separate release log, but will have a change implementation log, which includes all phases of the implementation.', 297),
    ('BAI07-WP11', 'BAI07', 'Supplemental support plan', 'Part of the implementation plans showing how users will be supported through the initial start-up phase and ongoing and how they will be supported. The length of the ongoing support will depend on the size and complexity of the changed system or process.', 298),
    ('BAI07-WP12', 'BAI07', 'Post-implementation review', 'Usually lags behind launch and support period. Assessors should confirm that it is planned.', 299),
    ('BAI07-WP13', 'BAI07', 'Remedial action plan', 'Part of the cutover planning; is important to ensure the support period of the implementation', 300),
    ('BAI08-WP1', 'BAI08', 'Classification of information sources', 'Similar to a data classification scheme, but enhanced for not only statutory requirements of data and record retention, but internal uses of information, taking into consideration knowledge database organisation', 301),
    ('BAI08-WP2', 'BAI08', 'Published knowledge repositories', 'Usually part of the web system combined with a repository (e.g., SharePoint), but specifically targeting public classified information', 302),
    ('BAI08-WP3', 'BAI08', 'Knowledge user database', 'A system like SharePoint or iMIS that the organisation will use or its user database', 303),
    ('BAI08-WP4', 'BAI08', 'Knowledge awareness and training schemes', 'Self-explanatory', 304),
    ('BAI08-WP5', 'BAI08', 'Knowledge use evaluation results', 'Enterprises should track the use of the knowledge database and capture or record the results.', 305),
    ('BAI08-WP6', 'BAI08', 'Rules for knowledge retirement', 'Part of the a knowledge strategy and plan that as part of a data classification and retention policy clarifies specific rules of retirement, which take into consideration legal and regulatory requirements', 306),
    ('BAI08-WP7', 'BAI08', 'Communications on value of knowledge', 'Part of the knowledge strategy and planning process', 307),
    ('BAI09-WP1', 'BAI09', 'Asset register', 'Asset registers are usually part of or integrated into the enterprise’s accounting software application and not normally found in separate IT registers. However, these systems will allow asset classifications to meet individual functional requirements such as the organisation of IT and information assets.', 308),
    ('BAI09-WP2', 'BAI09', 'Results of physical inventory checks', 'Physical inventories are usually conducted annually. It is important for IT to include this type of monitoring into its reporting process.', 309),
    ('BAI09-WP3', 'BAI09', 'Results of fit-for-purpose reviews', 'Review of IT assets in terms of meeting business requirements. It is a check for obsolescence and is important to ensure ongoing support for business or enterprise goals.', 310),
    ('BAI09-WP4', 'BAI09', 'Communication of planned maintenance downtime', 'An essential part of operational planning especially around databases, networks and critical applications', 311),
    ('BAI09-WP5', 'BAI09', 'Maintenance agreements', 'With vendors, but also with internal business users. Software licensing will be included in this process.', 312),
    ('BAI09-WP6', 'BAI09', 'Approved asset procurement requests', 'Part of the IT procurement process and usually linked to the purchase order/invoice matching process', 313),
    ('BAI09-WP7', 'BAI09', 'Updated asset register', 'Usually required when new or amended assets are added or made and part of the normal asset process', 314),
    ('BAI09-WP8', 'BAI09', 'Authorised asset retirements', 'Part of the normal assets management process and integrated into the accounting rules for assets retirement. Is not done in isolation of accounting policy and procedures.', 315),
    ('BAI09-WP9', 'BAI09', 'Results of cost optimisation reviews', 'Part of the assets monitoring and reporting process', 316),
    ('BAI09-WP10', 'BAI09', 'Opportunities to reduce asset costs or increase value', 'Part of the assets monitoring and reporting process', 317),
    ('BAI09-WP11', 'BAI09', 'Register of software licences', 'Assessors should verify the existence of a separate register of software licences because it is important for the audit process.', 318),
    ('BAI09-WP12', 'BAI09', 'Results of installed licence audits', 'Part of an audit report, usually annually', 319),
    ('BAI10-WP1', 'BAI10', 'Scope of configuration management model', 'Part of the actual configuration model. This is a detailed model of the IT infrastructure and how it relates to IT services.', 320),
    ('BAI10-WP2', 'BAI10', 'Logical configuration model', 'Self-explanatory; see scope explanation.', 321),
    ('BAI10-WP3', 'BAI10', 'Configuration repository', 'A database that holds the model, definitions, standards, etc.', 322),
    ('BAI10-WP4', 'BAI10', 'Configuration baseline', 'Part of the configuration model and repository. A baseline will be done at the development and planning stages.', 323),
    ('BAI10-WP5', 'BAI10', 'Updated repository with configuration items', 'Part of the maintenance process for configuration management', 324),
    ('BAI10-WP6', 'BAI10', 'Approved changes to baseline', 'Part of the maintenance process', 325),
    ('BAI10-WP7', 'BAI10', 'Configuration status reports', 'Part of the IT monitoring and reporting on configuration management', 326),
    ('BAI10-WP8', 'BAI10', 'Results of physical verification of configuration items', 'Part of the IT monitoring and reporting on configuration management', 327),
    ('BAI10-WP9', 'BAI10', 'Licence deviations', 'Where there are deviations on external licensing agreement, if applicable', 328),
    ('BAI10-WP10', 'BAI10', 'Results of repository completeness reviews', 'Part of the IT monitoring and reporting on configuration management', 329),
    ('DSS01-WP1', 'DSS01', 'Operational schedule', 'An IT operational schedule includes all IT services including outsourced, facilities management, infrastructure and environmental factors.', 330),
    ('DSS01-WP2', 'DSS01', 'Backup log', 'Part of data management. Assessors should check for operating practices/standards and/or policies for this.', 331),
    ('DSS01-WP3', 'DSS01', 'Asset monitoring rules and event conditions', 'Event conditions are part of comprehensive incident management, monitoring and reporting.', 332),
    ('DSS01-WP4', 'DSS01', 'Event logs', 'Same as for event conditions.', 333),
    ('DSS01-WP5', 'DSS01', 'Incident tickets', 'Part of the incident management and help desk system', 334),
    ('DSS01-WP6', 'DSS01', 'Environmental policies', 'Deals specifically with the management of IT environments, including data centers and storage rooms', 335),
    ('DSS01-WP7', 'DSS01', 'Insurance policy reports', 'Results of comparison of measures and contingency plans against insurance policy requirements', 336),
    ('DSS01-WP8', 'DSS01', 'Facilities assessment reports', 'Part of facilities management and physical risk assessments', 337),
    ('DSS01-WP9', 'DSS01', 'Health and safety awareness', 'Part of health safety and security environmental (HSSE) process and policies', 338),
    ('DSS01-WP10', 'DSS01', 'Independent assurance plans', 'Plans for independent audit and assurance of operational and HSSE activities, a critical part of a robust monitoring and reporting process.', 339),
    ('DSS02-WP1', 'DSS02', 'Incident and service request classification schemes and models', 'Part of the incident management process. Classifications schemes classifying the type of events/errors, etc., are a normal part of an incident management model.', 340),
    ('DSS02-WP2', 'DSS02', 'Rules for incident escalation', 'Part of the incident management model and process', 341),
    ('DSS02-WP3', 'DSS02', 'Criteria for problem registration', 'Part of the incident management model and process', 342),
    ('DSS02-WP4', 'DSS02', 'Incident and service request log', 'Part of the incident management model and process', 343),
    ('DSS02-WP5', 'DSS02', 'Classified and prioritised incidents and service requests', 'Part of the incident management model and process', 344),
    ('DSS02-WP6', 'DSS02', 'Approved service requests', 'Part of the incident management model and process', 345),
    ('DSS02-WP7', 'DSS02', 'Fulfilled service requests', 'Part of the incident management model and process', 346),
    ('DSS02-WP8', 'DSS02', 'Incident symptoms', 'Description of the issues that are caused by a certain problem', 347),
    ('DSS02-WP9', 'DSS02', 'Problem log', 'Separate to the incident log, but related', 348),
    ('DSS02-WP10', 'DSS02', 'Incident resolutions', 'Documented in an incident log. Assessors should check for alignment with the problem log.', 349),
    ('DSS02-WP11', 'DSS02', 'Closed service requests and incidents', 'Part of the incident logs', 350),
    ('DSS02-WP12', 'DSS02', 'User confirmation of satisfactory fulfillment or resolution', 'Part of the monitoring and reporting of incidents. Status reports should include user feedback/confirmation.', 351),
    ('DSS02-WP13', 'DSS02', 'Incident status and trends report', 'Part of the monitoring and reporting of incidents', 352),
    ('DSS02-WP14', 'DSS02', 'Request fulfilment status and trends report', 'Part of the monitoring and reporting of incidents', 353),
    ('DSS03-WP1', 'DSS03', 'Problem classification scheme', 'Similar to the incident classification, but specific to problems versus incidents', 354),
    ('DSS03-WP2', 'DSS03', 'Problem status reports', 'Part of the monitoring and reporting of problems and their status', 355),
    ('DSS03-WP3', 'DSS03', 'Problem register', 'Problems and their status are recorded; similar to an incident log or register', 356),
    ('DSS03-WP4', 'DSS03', 'Root causes of problems', 'Part of the problem register and ongoing problem management process', 357),
    ('DSS03-WP5', 'DSS03', 'Problem resolution reports', 'Part of the monitoring and reporting of problems and their status', 358),
    ('DSS03-WP6', 'DSS03', 'Known-error records', 'Source can be from incident logs and should be recorded in the problem register', 359),
    ('DSS03-WP7', 'DSS03', 'Proposed solutions to known errors', 'Found in the problem register', 360),
    ('DSS03-WP8', 'DSS03', 'Closed problem records', 'Found in the problem register', 361),
    ('DSS03-WP9', 'DSS03', 'Communication of knowledge learned', 'Part of the monitoring and reporting of problems and their status', 362),
    ('DSS03-WP10', 'DSS03', 'Problem resolution monitoring reports', 'Part of the monitoring and reporting of problems and their status', 363),
    ('DSS03-WP11', 'DSS03', 'Identified sustainable solutions', 'Part of the problem register', 364),
    ('DSS04-WP1', 'DSS04', 'Policy and objectives for business continuity', 'Can be found in an operating practice for business continuity and disaster recovery planning', 365),
    ('DSS04-WP2', 'DSS04', 'Disruptive incident scenarios', 'Part of the IT risk and enterprise risk management process', 366),
    ('DSS04-WP3', 'DSS04', 'Assessments of current continuity capabilities and gaps', 'Part of a comprehensive risk register. Some enterprises will keep a subregister of continuity gaps and capabilities.', 367),
    ('DSS04-WP4', 'DSS04', 'Business impact analyses', 'Part of the enterprise risk management system', 368),
    ('DSS04-WP5', 'DSS04', 'Continuity requirements', 'Specified as part of comprehensive business continuity plans (BCPs)/disaster recovery plans (DRPs)', 369),
    ('DSS04-WP6', 'DSS04', 'Approved strategic options', 'Specified as part of comprehensive BCPs/DRPs', 370),
    ('DSS04-WP7', 'DSS04', 'Incident response actions and communications', 'Specified as part of comprehensive BCPs/DRPs', 371),
    ('DSS04-WP8', 'DSS04', 'Business continuity plan', 'Self-explanatory, but will include links to emergency and incident management and IT DRPs', 372),
    ('DSS04-WP9', 'DSS04', 'Test objectives', 'Part of BCPs/DRPs', 373),
    ('DSS04-WP10', 'DSS04', 'Test exercises', 'Part of BCPs/DRPs', 374),
    ('DSS04-WP11', 'DSS04', 'Test results and recommendations', 'Part of the BCP monitoring and reporting process', 375),
    ('DSS04-WP12', 'DSS04', 'Results of reviews of plans', 'Part of the BCP monitoring and reporting process', 376),
    ('DSS04-WP13', 'DSS04', 'Recommended changes to plans', 'Part of the BCP monitoring and reporting process', 377),
